# Confirm before delete

Every **delete** action in the admin app must ask the user to confirm first, unless a task explicitly says to skip confirmation.

## Implementation

1. Use `ConfirmDeleteService` from `admin/src/app/core/confirm-delete.service.ts` (wraps PrimeNG `ConfirmationService`).
2. Ensure `<p-confirmDialog />` is present once in `shell.component.html` (app layout). Do not add duplicate confirm dialogs on feature pages.
3. `ConfirmationService` is provided in `app.config.ts`.

```typescript
import { ConfirmDeleteService } from '../../core/confirm-delete.service';

private readonly confirmDelete = inject(ConfirmDeleteService);

confirmDelete(item: Item) {
  this.confirmDelete.confirm({
    message: `Delete "${item.name}"? This cannot be undone.`,
    accept: async () => {
      await this.api.delete(`/items/${item.id}`);
      await this.load();
    },
  });
}
```

## Do not

- Call `api.delete()` directly from a button click without confirmation.
- Use `window.confirm()` — use the shared PrimeNG dialog for consistent UX.

## Row actions

Table delete menu items should call a `confirmDelete*` method, not delete inline. See `table-row-actions.mdc`.
